  "summary": "Malicious code in sme-rko-finance-front-operations-notifications-impl (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package downloads a platform-specific binary and executes it. It fetches the payload over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers hosts oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe depending on OS/arch. If the HTTP fetch fails, it falls back to a DNS-TXT channel: it queries c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (and ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru) for a TXT record giving a count, then fetches that many numbered TXT records, base64-decodes and reassembles the payload. The downloaded binary is written to a hidden file (.cache_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt; on Unix, dotnet_diag_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt;.exe on Windows) under /var/tmp or the temp dir, made executable, and launched detached via cmd.exe /c start /b (Windows) or /bin/sh -c \"\u0026lt;file\u0026gt; \u0026amp;\" (Unix).",
